This is not an assessment of your judgment. The bench results establish that the procedure worked on the tested hardware, firmware, and image. They do not establish that all 200 nodes have the same device mapping, mount state, disk capacity, or intact image.

My conclusion remains: **do not ship the original command as-is.** The minimum safeguards are:

- run from rescue/ramdisk;
- verify `/dev/nvme0n1` is the intended, unmounted target;
- ensure the image fits;
- force writes to complete;
- refresh and verify the partition state before resizing;
- confirm partition 1 contains ext4;
- deploy to 1 field node before the fleet.

If those checks cannot fit within the PXE window, extend the timeout or defer the broadcast. Bench success alone is insufficient evidence for an irreversible operation on 200 nodes.
